[RHYME SCHEMES - Notation System]

Pattern notation uses letters:
First unique sound = A
Second unique sound = B
Third unique sound = C
etc.

[AABB - COUPLET]
Line 1 (A)
Line 2 (A)
Line 3 (B)
Line 4 (B)

Example:
"I saw you walking in the rain" (A)
Our hearts would never be the same (A)
With every moment that we share (B)
I feel your love beyond compare (B)

Use: Folk, ballads, traditional
Effect: Predictable, satisfying rhythm

[ABAB - ALTERNATING]
Line 1 (A)
Line 2 (B)
Line 3 (A)
Line 4 (B)

Example:
"I'm climbing up this mountain high" (A)
With courage burning in my soul (B)
I'll reach the stars up in the sky" (A)
And finally become complete and whole (B)

Use: Pop, rock, contemporary
Effect: Dynamic, forward-moving feel

[ABCB - MIXED]
Line 1 (A)
Line 2 (B)
Line 3 (C)
Line 4 (B)

Example:
"She walked away into the night" (A)
Her silhouette fading away (B)
In my heart, she'll always stay (C)
I'll miss her light, I'll miss her way (B)

Use: Creative, unpredictable
Effect: Sophisticated, interesting

[AAAA - FULL CIRCLE]
All lines rhyme:

Example:
"I'm feeling free beneath the sky" (A)
With nothing standing in my way (A)
I'm reaching for my dreams so high (A)
Starting fresh this brand new day (A)

Use: Chorus, hooks, repetition
Effect: Very memorable, circular

[MULTI-LINE RHYME]
Extended rhyming across 5+ lines:

Example (AABBA):
"The morning sun is shining bright" (A)
I'm walking down this avenue" (A)
My spirit's feeling light" (B)
I feel like life is new (B)
And everything just feels so right" (A)

Use: Extended verses, storytelling
Effect: Complex, sophisticated

[RHYME PLACEMENT IN SONGS]

[End Rhyme]
Rhyme at end of lines (most common):
"I love to sing / The joy it brings"

[Internal Rhyme]
Rhyme within a line:
"I saw a ball fall in the hall"
"The dark mark made my heart ache"

[Multi-Position Rhyme]
Rhyming at multiple points:
"The bright light ignites the night"
(bright/light, ignites/night, light/night)

[RHYME MATCHING BY SYLLABLE COUNT]

Single syllable:
- sky / fly / high
- day / way / say
- free / be / see

Two syllables:
- broken / token / chosen
- shining / defining / combining
- ever / never / forever

Three+ syllables:
- tenderly / slenderly / wonderfully
- inspiration / dedication / elevation
- infinity / divinity / affinity

